RG DS OS: light both panels with the boot logo from U-Boot (docs/OWN_OS_PLAN.md, "U-Boot splash").

A minimal RK3566/RK3568 VOP2 driver (VP0 -> MIPI0 -> dsi0, the bottom screen; VP1 -> MIPI1 -> dsi1, the top
screen; an Esmart window each over one frame buffer), a driver for ROCKNIX's generic-dsi panels (panel_description
strings in the DT, as the kernel's panel-generic-dsi.c reads them), the rgds_splash command that brings them up from
bootcmd behind a fail-safe marker (/splash.log on the boot partition) and draws /splash.bmp, and the RG DS's panels,
supplies and backlights in the quartz64-a tree U-Boot runs. dw_mipi_dsi_rockchip.c takes each host's own panel and
DSI host child instead of the first in the system; the D-PHY driver is U-Boot's own.

